<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Artúr Görgei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1818">1818</a>–<a href="/years/1916">1916</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Arthur Görgey</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Artúr Görgei was the leading Hungarian general of the revolution of 1848–1849. His spring campaign of 1849 drove the Austrians back and recaptured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buda">Buda</a> in May. After the Russian intervention he surrendered the main Hungarian army at Világos in August 1849, for which many Hungarians long regarded him as a traitor.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/artur-gorgei.jpg" alt="Artúr Görgei" width="320" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Miklós Barabás · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:G%C3%B6rgei_Art%C3%BAr_portr%C3%A9.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
